  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The collection has enough variety for several suggestions, and guests may still request available games outside the suggested selection.\", \"decision\": \"How should games enter the evening’s suggested selection?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nGuests nominate games before the evening, and the host displays a varied selection from those nominations. The suggestions reflect known interest while leaving room for different playing times and levels of familiarity.\nGuests browse the collection on arrival and place interest markers beside games they would like to try. The suggested selection emerges from people present that evening rather than from earlier expectations about attendance.\nThe host displays suggested games after matching the collection with the evening’s available volunteer teachers. Guests see options that already have someone ready to explain them, reducing uncertainty about getting a game started."
    }
  ],
